\section{Conclusion}
In this work, we presented AdS, a novel parameter-efficient adapter-based framework for multimodal sarcasm detection. By limiting adapter placement to the upper layers of CLIP and introducing a text-to-image adapter-state sharing mechanism, AdS captures nuanced cross-modal sarcasm cues while maintaining low parameter overhead. Our method outperforms existing baselines and PEFT techniques, demonstrating that selective adapter placement and guided cross-modal interaction can significantly enhance performance in low-resource multimodal learning settings.



