There is a randomized algorithm that, given a set of $n$ red and blue points in the plane in general position, returns a plane bichromatic spanning tree of expected weight at most $O(\log n)$ times the optimum, and runs in $O(n\log^2 n)$ time. The algorithm can be derandomized by increasing the running time by a factor of $O(n^2)$.
