%怎么利用：在LLM里，有study直接用local window来加速，我们上面的观察说明在LMM里这个思路可行，所以我们也设计了local window来加速，发现性能没有大的损坏，但是加速能力有限。解释原因：因为kv-cache的存在，这些input只要算一遍，且对于LMM，他们处理long shot能力有限，所以提升速度能力不像能处理many shot的LLM那么有优势。但是至少证明了这样做的潜力，即未来有更强大的能够处理many shot的LMM时，local window加速的策略是有意义的。
When observing the attention maps when implementing ICL in LMM, we notice that in the middle layers, although we do not manually restrict each token in an ICE to attend only to tokens within the same ICE, it can be found that the tokens naturally attend to each other within the same ICE, with minimal interaction between ICEs as shown in Figure~\ref{fig:attention map} (d). We call this phenomenon the Emergent Attention Window.

To further quantitatively validate this phenomenon, we design an attention-based metric, Intra-Extra Attention Ratio (IEAR), to calculate the average ratio of the attention values within an ICE and between ICEs as shown in Figure\ref{fig:attention-based metric} (c): 
\begin{equation}
     \text{IEAR} = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{k=1}^{n} \frac{ \textbf{ATT} _{I}^{k} }{ \textbf{ATT} _{E}^{k} },
\end{equation}
\(\text{where } n \text{ represents the } n\text{-shot, }\)
\begin{equation}
\textbf{ATT} _{I}^{k} = \frac{1}{\left | S_{I}^{k} \right | }  {\textstyle \sum_{(i,j)\in S_{I}^{k}  }^{}A_{l}(i,j) } ,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
 S_{I}^{k} = \left \{ (i,j): i \in \mathcal{I}^{k}, j \in \mathcal{I}^{k} \right \} ,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\textbf{ATT} _{E}^{k} = \frac{1}{\left | S_{E}^{k} \right | } {\textstyle \sum_{(i,j)\in S_{E}^{k}  }^{}A_{l}(i,j) }  ,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
S_{E}^{k} = \left\{ (i,j) \mid i \in \mathcal{C} \setminus \mathcal{I}^{k}, j \in \mathcal{I}^{k} \right\} ,
\end{equation}
\(\text{where } \mathcal{I}^{k} \text{ represents the token set of the } k\text{-th ICE.}\)
Here, \(\textbf{ATT} _{I}^{k}\)  represents the average attention interaction of all context tokens within the k-th ICE, and \(\textbf{ATT} _{E}^{k}\) represents the average interaction between context tokens of other ICEs and those of the k-th ICE.
A higher IEAR value indicates more within-ICE interaction and less between-ICE interaction.



