We also emphasize that in the case of considering several cone constraints with distinct values of  $p_i=\frac{r_i}{s_i} \in \Q$, with $r_i > s_i\in \N^*$ and $\gcd(r_i,s_i)=1$, complexity estimates are obtained in a similar way as above, by simply replacing $r$ by $\max\{r_1,\dots,r_d\}$. 
