Inference efficiency is also crucial for matching models. Thus, we further compare the inference time of PERSCEN with other baselines on the Alimama test set. The experiments were conducted on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090Ti GPU with a batch size of 4096. 
Table~\ref{tab:infer} shows the average inference time per batch. 
The results indicate that PERSCEN’s inference time slightly increases compared to the baselines due to user-specific feature interaction modeling and scenario preference recognition. However, this increase is minor. 
