\mysubsection{Spatiotemporal sampling information}
We sampled arthropod communities at 19 sites in Sweden and northern Finland using Townes-style Malaise traps \cite{banelyte2023}. We deployed the traps continuously during 2021 and emptied them once per week. The MassID45 dataset we present here constitutes a subset of 45 of these samples, collected between March 31 and October 25, 2021 (Figure~\ref{fig:map}). Each sample is uniquely named with a six-character alphanumeric code and has associated geographic and temporal information, including the latitude and longitude of the sampling site, as well as placement and collection dates. 17 of the 19 sampling sites were part of a hierarchical sampling design \cite{hardwick2025} and were therefore clustered relatively closely together. In ecological analyses, this nested design allows us to compare samples which are close to each other (some $10^2$ m) to sites which are farther away ($10^6$ m) through a range of scales (Figure~\ref{fig:map}). After collection, samples were shipped to the Centre for Biodiversity Genomics, Guelph, Canada, where they were preserved in fresh 96\% ethanol and stored at --20°C until analysis. 

