\section{Conclusion}

\label{conclusion}
In this paper, we primarily studied $2$-to-$1$ polynomials of the form $F(x)=G(x)+\tr_{q^l/q}(R(x))$, where  $q=2^k$, $G(x)$ is a monomial and $R(x)$ is a monomial or binomial. Starting from the properties of $2$-to-$1$ mappings, we first utilized MAGMA to search for specific $2$-to-$1$ polynomials data generated by different values of $k$ and $l$ over small fields. By employing the elementary method, combining the properties of Dickson polynomials, and the Dobbertin's multivariate method, we constructed $16$ new infinite classes of $2$-to-$1$ polynomials, which include $9$ classes of $R(x)$ that are monomials and $7$ classes of $R(x)$ that are binomials. Finally, some binary self-orthogonal and minimal linear codes with few weights are provided, implying our constructions of $2$-to-$1$ mappings are useful. Note that the $2$-to-$1$ mappings proposed in this paper can also be applied to constructing balanced Boolean functions as done in  \cite{qu2025parametric}. 

