\subsection{Training Regimes and Early Stopping}

Training was conducted in two phases: (1) 100 epochs with image and message losses, followed by (2) 20 epochs with added physics loss. Early stopping was based on validation image loss, provided decoder accuracy exceeded 98\%.

\noindent\textit{Note:} Epochs are zero-indexed in our training logs. For example, “early stop after 82 epochs” means training was halted at Epoch 81.

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Fluid Flow:} Early stopping at epoch 81 (phase 1) and epoch 19 (phase 2).
    \item \textbf{ERA5:} Early stopping at epoch 90 (phase 1) and epoch 16 (phase 2).
    \item \textbf{Cosmology:} Trained for 50 epochs, early stopping at epoch 33.
\end{itemize}

