\section{Map Generation by Triangle Subdivision}

The first step is to present a simple map generation method using
triangular subdivision.  We use isosceles, right-angled triangles as
shown in Figure~\ref{triangle}(a).  We divide this into two half-size
triangle by drawing a new edge $e_3$ from the vertex $V_0$ to the middle of the
opposite edge $e_0$, splitting this into two new edges $e_4$ and
$e_5$, as shown in Figure~\ref{triangle}(b).  The new vertex at the
middle of $e_0$ is called $V_3$.

