Figure \ref{fig:violin_picture} presents the violin plots of bug open duration, number of comments, and patch size. Colossal-AI exhibits shorter bug open durations than DeepSpeed and Megatron-LM, possibly because developers promptly address issues upon reporting, which correlates with fewer comments per issue. However, all three frameworks show similar patch sizes, with medians ranging from 8 to 14 LOC. Following previous work~\cite{wang2021exploratory,yang2025towards}, we analyze bug-labeled issues that remain open for over one month and receive more than ten comments, comprising approximately 6\% of all cases. These prolonged issues reflect substantial debugging effort. Through analyzing these cases, we identify three major challenges in pinpointing the root causes of bugs in the frameworks. 

% https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/issues/2911
% 定位 BUG 的难度通常在其表现症状与根本成因无直接关联时显著增加。以 DeepSpeed #2911 为例，用户反馈的 BUG 症状为：在 bf16 或 fp32 模式下，系统日志输出损失缩放器相关警告，但实际未启用该功能。初步排查推测是日志模块异常，经社区多名开发者一起讨论分析，发现核心成因是框架分布式通信中 bf16 状态下传递 fp16 类型数据，导致梯度计算出现无限值，触发警告逻辑。
\textbf{The Disconnect Between Bug Symptoms and Causes}: The difficulty of locating bugs often increases significantly when symptoms show no direct correlation with root causes. For example, in DeepSpeed Issue \textit{\#2911}~\cite{deepspeed2911}, users reported bf16/fp32 mode system logs showed loss scaler warnings despite the feature being off. Initially, the issue proposer suspected a warning module anomaly. However, joint analysis by community developers revealed the core problem: fp16 data was transmitted in a bf16 state during distributed communication, causing infinite gradient values that triggered the warning. 


